# Third-party attribution — envoy-modsec-connex

This project is an Envoy **External Processing (`ext_proc`)** connector to
**libmodsecurity** (ModSecurity v3). It is **not** affiliated with or endorsed by
the Envoy, ModSecurity, OWASP CRS, or Built on Envoy projects.

## Envoy

- Project: [envoyproxy/envoy](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy)
- Relevant API: External Processor (`envoy.service.ext_proc.v3`)
- Typical license: Apache License 2.0
- This repository implements a client of that API; Envoy itself is not vendored here.

## ModSecurity / libmodsecurity

- Project: [owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity](https://github.com/owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity)
- Typical license: Apache License 2.0
- Runtime dependency when the connector links against libmodsecurity.

## OWASP Core Rule Set (CRS)

- Project: [coreruleset/coreruleset](https://github.com/coreruleset/coreruleset)
- Typical license: Apache License 2.0
- CRS rule packs are **optional** for engine/connector development and must be
  fetched/attributed separately when used. Do not treat CRS as bundled unless a
  future release explicitly vendors it with license compliance.

## Built on Envoy (BoE)

- Docs: https://builtonenvoy.io/
- Catalog / examples: [tetratelabs/built-on-envoy](https://github.com/tetratelabs/built-on-envoy)
- This repo targets BoE `type: ext_proc` alignment for a **future** catalog path.
  **No catalog submission** has been made from this repository.

## Coraza (reference only)

- Coraza and its Envoy connectors are studied for body/EOS design lessons only.
- This product ships **libmodsecurity**, not Coraza.

